+# Native query observations — local synthetic source only
+
+Observed on macOS 27.0 / 26A428, arm64, development 0.1.0, schema 15. App identifier `dev.hmrguez.gitjuke.queryqualification`, window **GitJuke Queries — LOCAL SYNTHETIC SOURCE**. Configured window 1280×800; no minimum-content-size, text-zoom or performance measurement is claimed. The app uses real WebKit/Tauri/IPC/Rust/SQLite and an explicitly configured local Python gh helper. No GitHub connection, credential access/change or remote fixture creation occurred.
+
+1. Fresh app showed **New query**, no saved entries, **Paused**, and identity-gated cached content. The preparer created no query definition. Native **Refresh pull requests** validated local identity `github.com / reader / 42` and showed the complete empty authored set.
+2. **New query** → name **Local review desk**, search **repo:a/b is:open** → **Save query**. Native results showed **100 cached · 150 reported by GitHub · Incomplete cached set**, with page-one PR rows.
+3. Clicked **My PRs**, then the persisted **Local review desk** primary-navigation entry. The query and its results reopened.
+4. Scrolled the query navigator and activated **Next results**. The UI showed **150 cached · 150 reported by GitHub · Complete cached set**, **Page 2**, rows **#101–#150**, enabled Previous and disabled Next.
+5. Opened **a/b · #101 Change 101**. The normal Overview reader displayed **Change 101**, `reader · main ← aaaaaaaaaa` and the literal plain-text body `<script>untrusted</script>`. The reader subsequently reported no published stack. No GitHub-source action was activated. A screenshot was inspected in the native-tool conversation; no screenshot file is claimed in this evidence directory.
+6. Cmd-Q/relaunch retained query ID 1, its search, local helper/configuration paths and Pause. The new session gated fetched content until local identity validation. The prior PR selection reopened through the normal reader.
+7. Native **Edit query** restored both fields. After the initial-focus correction, the accessibility tree explicitly reported focus on **Name**, value **Local review desk**. A select-all/type attempt appended text; that intermediate save produced version 2. The native AX setter corrected the name to **Local review desk renamed**, and Return submitted version 3. Only Name focus and Return submission are qualified; native select-all/menu shortcut behavior remains unqualified.
+8. After another full restart into the final artifact, primary navigation retained **Local review desk renamed** before identity validation. Explicit Refresh/reselection fetched version-three page one with **100 cached / 150 reported / incomplete**. Next results fetched its second page and restored **150 cached / 150 reported / complete**. Selecting #101 again rendered **Change 101** and the literal body through the standard reader. Final source artifact/hash is recorded in `artifact.json`.
+
+Read-only SQLite captures: `native-before-restart.json` and `native-after-restart.json`. They preserve query ID 1 and search, version 1→3, Pause and helper/config paths, stable fixture identity 42, exact 100/50 cached pages per run, and the selected PR cache. Only `PR_101 / selected` is a watch reason; the other 149 query results never enrolled. Older version-one pages remain disposable cache payloads but cannot be read through the current version-three query IPC. Thirteen assertions over these captured metadata stages pass in `observation-verification.json`; that is an evidence check, not an unattended fresh UI test.
+
+During concurrent local qualification, low free space stopped further native query reads under the existing guard. This task reclaimed its own disposable build clone and left the production threshold unchanged. A discovered frontend error-clearing bug was corrected: cached rereads no longer erase failed fetch messages, and the query view now surfaces runtime storage health. The new mounted test qualifies that error display. No controlled native disk-boundary fault matrix or complete protective-state screenshot is claimed. Fresh native version-three reads succeeded after space/repair recovered.
+
+Native deletion, negative/partial/quota/race permutations, long/max-byte names and results, >100 query navigation, compact/200%/VoiceOver/reduced motion and physical-target performance were not exercised here. They retain deterministic coverage where recorded or remain Pending. The normal app/account was not configured or launched by this qualification. No notifications, login registration, signing, publication or distribution was enabled. All 29 grouped release scenarios remain Pending.
